# Templates

A `.rocci` file is HTML for Roc. You declare a PascalCase `@component`,
it lowers to a pure function that returns `Html`, and you preview it
without a server.

Until an installed `rocci` exists, prefix each `rocci` command with
`cargo run -q -p rocci-cli --` from the repository root.

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/components/", title: "Components", summary: "Declare, call, preview, and fixtures."]
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/markup/", title: "Markup", summary: "Tags, attributes, interpolations, scoped CSS, stable ids."]
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/directives/", title: "Directives", summary: "@if, @for, @match, @let."]
:card-grid.end

Stop here if you only preview components into an existing `main.roc`. You
do not need Applications until you want generated dispatch or you own
routing yourself.

Exact forms: [language reference](/docs/reference/language/).
When you need HTTP: [Applications](/docs/applications/).
